Benchmark 2: Compute-Heavy (N = 2^24 elements, 64-iteration inner loop)
  - PTX Instruction Counts:
      MiniPTX:                           54 instructions
      CUDA (nvcc -O3):                   28 instructions
      CUDA no-FMA (nvcc --fmad=false):   29 instructions
  - Measured Runtime (Median):
      MiniPTX:                           0.4874 ms (4405.8 GFLOPS)
      CUDA (nvcc -O3):                   0.4342 ms (4946.1 GFLOPS)
      CUDA no-FMA (nvcc --fmad=false):   0.4884 ms (4396.5 GFLOPS)
  - Measured Ratios:
      MiniPTX / CUDA (nvcc -O3):         1.123x (12.26% slower)
      MiniPTX / CUDA no-FMA:             0.998x (0.21% diff, exact match within noise)
      CUDA (nvcc -O3) vs CUDA no-FMA:    0.889x (11.11% speedup from hardware FMA fusion)

SASS Machine Instruction & Opcode Breakdown (Compute-Heavy):
  - MiniPTX (emitted PTX):
      Total SASS instructions:           24
      Opcode breakdown:                  FFMA: 0 | FMUL: 1 | FADD: 1
      Loop structure:                    Rolled loop (unroll factor 1: 2 float ops in body, 1 branch)
  - CUDA (nvcc -O3):
      Total SASS instructions:           32
      Opcode breakdown:                  FFMA: 1 | FMUL: 0 | FADD: 0
      Loop structure:                    Rolled loop (unroll factor 1: 1 float op in body, 1 branch)
  - CUDA no-FMA (nvcc --fmad=false):
      Total SASS instructions:           32
